WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.917
A truck delivers one thousand kilograms of
potatoes. The supplier calls this lot
POT-2601.

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:13.049
The plant assigns production batch FRY-1001.

00:00:13.094 --> 00:00:22.273
Keep both identifiers: one identifies the
incoming material, the other the work
performed.

00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:25.861
We will follow that link from receiving
through control,

00:00:25.906 --> 00:00:28.640
packing and inventory reconciliation.

00:00:29.465 --> 00:00:33.980
The receiving operator matches the delivery to
its purchase reference

00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:38.284
and checks gross weight minus tare against the
measured net mass.

00:00:38.459 --> 00:00:45.019
The manufacturing execution system, or MES,
records the supplier lot on hold.

00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:49.754
A matching inspection result and confirmed
put-away release the material.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:53.378
Advanced planning and scheduling, or APS,

00:00:53.423 --> 00:00:57.128
can then reserve line capacity for that
released order.

00:00:57.173 --> 00:00:59.938
A reservation does not start the conveyor.

00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:03.482
The physical plan answers "where?"

00:01:03.527 --> 00:01:07.796
It locates the detector and the controller
input at the packing cell.

00:01:07.841 --> 00:01:10.858
Check the actual connection at the equipment.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:14.664
The logical view asks "what must communicate?"

00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:20.333
The controller sends the carton-present tag
through a switch to the supervisory server.

00:01:20.508 --> 00:01:23.439
A diagram line does not prove the cable,

00:01:23.484 --> 00:01:27.390
the received optical light level or a healthy
application.

00:01:27.435 --> 00:01:33.832
Check the link and optical reading, then
verify tag value, quality and sample time.

00:01:34.657 --> 00:01:41.645
The controller requests conveyor motion. A run
command means the program asked for motion.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:45.308
The drive feedback tells us what actually
happened.

00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:47.821
With command on and feedback off,

00:01:47.866 --> 00:01:53.369
the operator checks the permissives and the
drive status before assuming the belt moved.

00:01:53.544 --> 00:02:00.325
The supervisory control and data acquisition
system, or SCADA, displays both signals.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.515
The historian records their time sequence.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.179
Look at two samples. The first detector reads
zero,

00:02:09.224 --> 00:02:16.178
with good quality and a current timestamp.
That is evidence of no carton at that sample.

00:02:16.353 --> 00:02:22.066
The second display also shows zero, but its
timestamp has stopped advancing.

00:02:22.111 --> 00:02:24.778
The current detector state is unknown.

00:02:24.953 --> 00:02:31.152
Compare the source and server timestamps,
communication quality and last change.

00:02:31.197 --> 00:02:34.841
A steady process can still produce fresh
samples.

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:38.811
The packing scale records seven hundred

00:02:38.856 --> 00:02:43.747
and forty-four kilograms of finished fries
against FRY-1001.

00:02:43.922 --> 00:02:48.599
That is a packed-to-raw ratio of seventy-four
point four per cent.

00:02:48.644 --> 00:02:51.653
The difference is not automatically scrap.

00:02:51.828 --> 00:02:58.474
Reconcile the stage records: potato input plus
measured additions must equal packed output

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:03.637
plus recorded removals. MES keeps the lot
genealogy.

00:03:04.462 --> 00:03:10.509
The enterprise resource planning system, SAP,
receives the packed-stock posting.

00:03:10.554 --> 00:03:14.701
Suppose the acknowledgement is lost after the
posting succeeds.

00:03:14.876 --> 00:03:19.391
The interface retries the same event
identifier and quantity.

00:03:19.436 --> 00:03:24.414
The receiver recognises the original posting
and returns its acknowledgement.

00:03:24.589 --> 00:03:28.694
Inventory remains seven hundred and forty-four
kilograms.

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:35.040
Verify one movement, one event key, and a
trace from finished batch back to supplier
lot.
